跨国反腐
China's plan to enact a law against cross-border corruption is an essential step to improve its domestic anti-graft legal system and also a crucial move to enrich its legislative toolbox related to foreign affairs. Transnational corruption includes premeditation and collusion before a corrupt act is committed, as well as asset transfers or money laundering after the act. The law, while advancing pursuits, will also help regulate the integrity of our country's businesses in international commercial activities, strengthen our exchanges in law enforcement with relevant counties and deepen our global cooperation combating corruption.